(ESCALATION AND DELINQUENCY POLICY \(Sample, fictional\)) Tj T*
(Policy ID: ES-03) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. Delinquency stages) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(An account is in Stage 1 when it is 1 to 30 days overdue, Stage 2 when it is 31 to 60) Tj T*
(days overdue, Stage 3 when it is 61 to 90 days overdue, and Stage 4 when it is more than) Tj T*
(90 days overdue.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2. Actions by stage) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In Stage 1 the customer receives a reminder message and no late fee is charged during) Tj T*
(the first 10 days. In Stage 2 a collections officer must attempt a live phone) Tj T*
(conversation and must offer to discuss a hardship plan. In Stage 3 the account is) Tj T*
(assigned to a named collections officer and a formal notice of arrears is sent by post.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
