stream
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 760 Td 14 TL
(3. Escalation to a human reviewer) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Every account that reaches Stage 4, meaning more than 90 days overdue, must be escalated) Tj T*
(to a human collections officer before any legal notice is sent. An automated agent must) Tj T*
(also escalate to a human when the customer disputes the debt, when the customer mentions) Tj T*
(bankruptcy or a lawyer, when the outstanding balance is above 25,000 dollars, or when) Tj T*
(the agent's confidence in its recommended action is low.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(4. Legal action) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Legal action may only be started on accounts in Stage 4 and requires written approval) Tj T*
(from the Head of Collections. Legal action must not be started while a hardship plan is) Tj T*
(active or while a dispute is open.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(5. Record keeping) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Each escalation must record the reason, the date, the officer who accepted it, and the) Tj T*
(outcome. Records are kept for seven years.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
